  "author": "Dr. Angela Thorne, Astronomy Education Lead",
  "courseName": "Introduction to Astronomy (ASTR 101)",
  "estimatedLength": "40 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Describe the apparent path of Mars across the night sky during a retrograde episode, including its speed changes and direction reversals.",
    "Explain why apparent retrograde motion occurs in a heliocentric model as a natural consequence of Earth overtaking a slower outer planet.",
    "Contrast geocentric epicyclic explanations with heliocentric geometric explanations for planetary loops.",
    "Predict retrograde occurrences based on the relative orbital configurations of Earth and outer planets.",
    "Compare retrograde loops of Mars, Jupiter, and Saturn to understand how distance affects the angular size of the loop."
